    "cleaning_guide": {
      "type": "infographic",
      "blocks": {
        "row_1": {
          "type": "media_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Beginner's scrub",
            "text": "<p>Dissolve one tablespoon of mild dish soap into a glass of warm water and let your jewelry go for a little swim. Scrub gently with a soft cloth or an old soft-bristle toothbrush before rinsing with clean water.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Beginners_Scrub.jpg",
            "image_mobile": "shopify://shop_images/Beginners_Scrub_41c165f3-bef8-417a-9a80-5156b786e923.jpg"
          }
        },
        "row_2": {
          "type": "media_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Zen clean",
            "text": "<p>Add 3 drops of lemon essential oil to a half cup of witch hazel or vinegar. Let your jewelry sit for 5 minutes, and wipe with a soft polishing cloth if necessary. Rinse with clean water.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Zen_Clean.jpg",
            "image_mobile": "shopify://shop_images/Zen_Clean_d2630cbf-3cd8-4b73-9c08-71841704607b.jpg"
          }
        },
        "row_3": {
          "type": "media_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "For plated pieces",
            "text": "<p>When treating plated pieces, gentleness is key. Do not scrub or use a polishing cloth as this will damage the coating. Rub the surface gently with a soft jewelry cloth.</p><p>Photo by <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@tanyatrukyr\" target=\"_blank\">Tanya Trukyr</a> on <a href=\"https://unsplash.com\" target=\"_blank\">Unsplash</a></p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/For_Plated_Pieces.jpg",
            "image_mobile": "shopify://shop_images/For_Plated_Pieces_d3ec7109-f923-41ec-a97f-646b42764d7b.jpg"
          }
        },
        "row_4": {
          "type": "media_text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "For raw brass and sterling silver jewelry polish finish",
            "text": "<p>Make a paste using half a lemon and a teaspoon of baking soda. Rub the paste in your jewelry in one direction with a cotton cloth. Wipe off and rinse.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Raw_Brass.jpg",
            "image_mobile": "shopify://shop_images/Raw_Brass_65cea7ce-50fc-40c2-b1f6-e7720dbe7fc1.jpg"
          }
        }
      },
